new file mode 100644
index 0000000..848cafd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/vu0-native.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Native VU0 microprograms
+
+VU0 keeps the reference interpreter's truncating arithmetic and externally visible final MAC/status flags. It uses a separate program registry, 4 KiB code/data masks and a generation cache. VU1's vector arithmetic and keys are unchanged. The generator ABI fingerprint has been bumped so old live libraries are rebuilt.
+
+Unknown VU0 programs run in the exact interpreter. `PS2_VU0_RECORD=<directory>` records their 4 KiB code images using the existing key/entry filename convention. Compile recordings with:
+
+```
+vurecomp <vu1-directory> <generated-directory> --vu0-dir <vu0-directory>
+```
+
+`port.sh` also records and compiles `games/<id>/vu0`. The normal runner does not compile VU0 on the fly. Entries with unsupported instructions, register jumps or XGKICK remain entirely interpreted, preserving the pipeline and avoiding duplicate external side effects during verification.
+
+- `PS2_VU0_INTERPRET=1`: force the exact interpreter for A/B comparisons.
+- `PS2_VU0_VERIFY=1`: compare every compiled call with exact interpretation from identical registers and memory. Compare the entire register structure, including TPC, and all 4096 data bytes. Keep the reference result and blacklist an entry on mismatch.
+- `PS2_VU0_STATS=1`: report compiled/interpreted counts every million calls. The final atexit report is available to hosts that exit normally; the window host uses `_Exit`.
+
+Run `python3 scripts/test_vu0_codegen.py` without a game disc. It reuses the shared synthetic instruction fixtures to check 150 random programs and the pipeline cases, full state, code/data wrapping, final flags without a reader, a zero destination mask, per-unit key isolation, code replacement, unknown/register-jump fallback, and a deliberately wrong function to exercise verification and blacklisting. `python3 scripts/test_vu_codegen.py` retains the native VU1 and Wasm regressions.
+
+Local SC3 validation: seven recorded VU0 entries compiled; a complete 5538-frame input replay checked at least 14,940,000 compiled calls with zero state mismatches. The input recording itself has a pre-existing hash divergence at frame 1875, so this is a call-level semantic check, not a claim that the old input recording reproduced the original run exactly. Generated game code, recordings, memory cards and measurement files are kept outside the source patch.
